    "facts": "This is an application for bail under Section\n438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure.\nIt is asserted in the FIR that the informant received an information that contraband articles namely, Gutka, Pan Masala,\nscented beetle nuts, etc., were being transported in a vehicle.\nCommission of the alleged offence is an anti-social act.\n",
    "arguments": "He, therefore,\nurged for grant of anticipatory bail.\n",
    "ANALYSIS": "6. Admittedly, the above-mentioned contraband articles came to be seized from the vehicle.\nThere is, prima facie, nothing to indicate that accused Manik had bought those article from the applicant,\nexcept the bare words of Manik.\n7. In my view, Section 328 of the I.P.C. has no application.\nSo is not a case here.\nRest of the offences in the present FIR are bailable.\n8. The allegations in the FIR do not indicate the applicant to have administered the said article to anyone.\nThe offence under Sections 188, 272 and 273 of Indian Penal Code are bailable.\nSo far as the offences under the F.S.S. Act are concerned, it is observed that there is no C.A. report.\nCompliance of Section 42 of the F.S.S. Act is, prima facie, not evident.\n",
